	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tbP3FTIIGxwyfP3EG",
			"name": "Wealthy",
			"reference": "B25",
			"local_notes": "5x average TL2 starting wealth ($750 x5 = $3,750). Her personal allowance/dowry-portion, distinct from House Dustin's own treasury -- see Financial Position note below.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"calc": {
				"points": 20
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "tHPnMWgRxKbCo3jMc",
			"name": "Status",
			"reference": "B28",
			"local_notes": "2 levels, 5 pts/level. Typical Wealth for Status 2 is Wealthy (B517 correspondence table), so this pairing needs no debt or special pleading. Cost of living $3,000/month (B265), paid by House Dustin, not from her personal Wealthy money.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social"
			],
			"base_points": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2,
			"calc": {
				"points": 10,
				"current_level": 2
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "tjMKt67ML_MdaQHZk",
			"name": "Common Sense",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "The mechanical form of her political caution -- the GM warns her before she does something the GM considers stupid. Not a reaction bonus; keeps her social competence grounded in judgment, per the brief's instruction that her abilities come from intelligence and training, not charm.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental"
			],
			"base_points": 10,
			"calc": {
				"points": 10
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "t1dxSksNrmQPL8j8F",
			"name": "Stubbornness",
			"reference": "B157",
			"local_notes": "Required trait. Others react at -1. Roleplay: once judgment, competence, or inheritance is challenged, she has real difficulty backing down.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental"
			],
			"base_points": -5,
			"calc": {
				"points": -5
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "tj1T_niDyhquPNteH",
			"name": "Social Stigma (Second-Class Citizen)",
			"reference": "B155-156",
			"local_notes": "Sex-based, per Social Engineering p.16's explicit category (\"Second-Class Citizen, if based on sex\"). -1 on reaction rolls from men who won't take her seriously as heir-material. Political and dynastic, not universal contempt -- her Status 2 is untouched and does separate work. Direct RAW precedent: B28, \"a woman could have high Status, but still get -1 on reactions due to the Social Stigma of being female.\"",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social"
			],
			"base_points": -5,
			"calc": {
				"points": -5
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "txCu_wmgjxavMkw9V",
			"name": "Sense of Duty (Family)",
			"reference": "B153",
			"local_notes": "Small Group. Self-imposed, not externally assigned -- this is the correct trait rather than Duty (B133 excludes wholly self-imposed obligation). Grounds her stated warmth and sincere concern for Barrowton's people in an actual character-point trait.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental"
			],
			"base_points": -5,
