	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nLlPZclxITBCkrPZW",
			"markdown": "**SELF-DEFENSE DOCTRINE** -- survive -> create an opening -> disengage -> escape -> reach guards/allies (per design brief). She never intends to finish a fight herself.\n\n1. Grab/drag: Wrestling-11 to control the limb or break free; going limp and loud if dragged.\n2. Trapped, no grab yet: Stealth-10 and Body Language/Observation-15 should have already prevented this. Knife-10 via Fast-Draw-10 as a visible deterrent, not to fight.\n3. Successfully grappled an attacker: Choke Hold-11 restrains and chokes to unconsciousness, then she leaves.\n4. Armed opponent: she does not close. Reach C,1 on the knife cannot out-range a real weapon. Stall with Fast-Talk/Diplomacy and look for the exit.\n5. Opening appears: Stealth and Running carry her out. This is the win condition.\n\nFull build rationale, source citations, and the point-by-point account: characters/dustin/canon/Alys_Dustin_GURPS_Character.md."
		},
		{
			"id": "nv6pUL0xN1xhKNfqp",
			"markdown": "**THE MORMONT BETROTHAL -- no trait purchased, purely narrative.** Checked against Ally (B36-37), Patron (B72), and Contact (B42-44): none fit a fiance who lives on Bear Island, runs his own house's business, and is not yet resident with her -- none of the three mechanics' availability requirements are met. Same reasoning clears her brother (not an Enemy -- no hostile intent; not a Dependent -- he isn't weaker or in her care) and her father (the source of her education, which is why her skill list is what it is, not an in-play Contact -- she already has the skills herself). Full argument: canon doc §L."
		},
		{
			"id": "nu3k79KnUtcFuEMn6",
			"markdown": "**FINANCIAL POSITION.** Wealthy [20] = personal starting money of $3,750 (5x TL2 average of $750, B27) -- hers, not House Dustin's. Status 2 costs $3,000/month to maintain (Cost of Living Table, B265), paid by the House, not deducted from her personal cash. The castle, the grain monopoly, the staff, and the guards are accessed through Status 2 and family position, not owned via any purchased trait -- charging her personally for any of it would double-count what Status and Wealthy already represent."
		}
	],
